<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Caizhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1233–<a href="/years/1234">1234</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-conquest-of-the-jin-dynasty">Mongol conquest of the Jin dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Caizhou in 1233 and 1234 was the final campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Mongol forces and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> army besieged Emperor Aizong in the city of Caizhou in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, which fell in February 1234. Aizong killed himself and his short-lived successor was killed in the fighting, ending the Jin dynasty.</p></div>
